            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Vigorous, thornless. Fruit: Large size, firm, black, very uniform shape, good flavor. Yield: High. Market: Fresh or processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 1"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Columbia Star",
            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Very vigorous, thornless. Fruit: Large size, firm, very uniform shape, outstanding flavor and processing quality. Yield: High. Market: Fresh or processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Comment: Too new for the 2014 PDF table to fully evaluate but very promising; source table names this as Columbia Star (U.S. Plant Patent pending)"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Kotata",
            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Very vigorous, very thorny. Fruit: Small to medium size, good firmness, dark purple, uniform shape, excellent flavor. Yield: Medium. Market: Fresh or processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Comment: May be difficult to market processed but popular for fresh market"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Marion",
            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Very vigorous, thorny. Fruit: Medium size, soft, dark purple, uneven shape, excellent flavor. Yield: Medium. Market: Processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 1. Comment: Source table notes this is often called marionberry"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Wild Treasure",
            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Thornless, very vigorous. Thin canes break easily, so commercial growers should use alternate-year production systems or train canes very gently to avoid breakage. Fruit: Small size, medium firmness, dark purple, very uniform shape, excellent flavor. Yield: Low to high, depending on amount of damage during cane training. Market: Processed, particularly small fruit market. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Small farm or home garden: Suited for small fruit market"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Onyx",
            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Vigorous, thorny, fairly upright growth habit for a trailing blackberry. Fruit: Medium size, uniform shape, firm, black, excellent sweet, mild flavor. Yield: Medium. Market: Fresh. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Comment: Too new for the 2014 PDF table to fully evaluate but expected to do well in fresh market; source table names this as Onyx (U.S. Plant Patent 22,358)"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Thornless Evergreen",
            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "August-September",
            description: "Plant: Vigorous, thornless. Fruit: Small size, soft, black, mild but good flavor, August-September ripening season, prone to gray mold after fall rains. Yield: High. Market: Processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Comment: Nursery plants not available; source describes this as a thornless chimera and combines it in one table row with Everthornless"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Everthornless",
            category: "Trailing blackberries for Oregon",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "August-September",
            description: "Plant: Vigorous, thornless. Fruit: Small size, soft, black, mild but good flavor, August-September ripening season, prone to gray mold after fall rains. Yield: High. Market: Processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Comment: Nursery plants not available; source describes this as a genetically thornless clone and combines it in one table row with Thornless Evergreen"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Logan",
            category: "Blackberry/red raspberry hybrids for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Moderate vigor, thorny, canes susceptible to disease. Thornless Logan is available, but it is not genetically thornless and will produce thorny canes. Fruit: Medium size, more like raspberry than blackberry in color and flavor, deep red color, conic shape, excellent firmness but tender skin, excellent but distinctive flavor, hard to pick. Yield: Low to medium. Market: Processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Comment: Source table notes this is often called loganberry"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Tayberry",
            category: "Blackberry/red raspberry hybrids for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Moderate vigor, thornless. Fruit: Medium size, glossy, reddish purple, good firmness but tender skin, excellent but unique tart flavor, very hard to pick, fruit damaged easily by hot weather. Yield: Low. Market: Processed. Large-scale commercial value rating: 3. Comment: Successful niche markets have been developed, but low yield and difficulty of harvest make this nearly impossible to produce economically"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
            name: "Newberry",
            category: "Blackberry/red raspberry hybrids for Oregon",
            description: "Plant: Vigorous, thorny. Fruit: Large size, blocky, glossy, reddish purple to dark purple, firmer and tougher skin than Boysen, excellent flavor, but despite Boysen look, does not have Boysen flavor. Yield: Very high. Market: Fresh. Large-scale commercial value rating: 2. Comment: Too new for the 2014 PDF table to fully evaluate"
        },
        {
            type: "Blackberry",
